CoreFoundation compiled as Objective-C dispatches to Objective-C objects
passed to CF functions, as Apple's does: CFInternal.h takes the dispatch
macros from userland/CoreFoundation/CFObjCDispatch_Finch.h; the generic
calls (CFRetain, CFRelease, CFGetRetainCount, CFCopyDescription,
CFGetAllocator) and CFArrayGetValueAtIndex get their ObjC paths back;
retyping an instance (CFDictionary, CFSet, stack keys) and static instances
set the ObjC class; and two declarations that clash with ObjC are skipped.
_CFArrayIsMutable, _CFDataIsMutable and _CFCharacterSetIsMutable are for the
classes of those objects; __CFStringIsMutable is Apple's export, for Foundation.


